      transcriptEN: 'You have seen the whole machine; the last step is to wire it yourself. Open the workbench and build one controlled-subtractor cell: two cascaded XORs for the difference, an inverter plus three ANDs plus an OR for the borrow, and a 2-to-1 MUX with select equal to the borrow, I0 the difference, I1 the original minuend. Drive the inputs and watch it behave: when the subtraction fits, borrow is 0, the MUX passes the difference, quotient bit 1; when it underflows, borrow is 1, the MUX restores the minuend, quotient bit 0. Once one cell is solid, tiling is mechanical - chain the borrow across to make a row, broadcast the row sign as the select, feed each output down to the next row, and stack n rows for a complete divider.',
